<title>USA: Two NETCOM board members resign.</title>
<headline>Two NETCOM board members resign.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>NETCOM On-Line Communication Services Inc Tuesday said two board members have stepped down, reducing the size of the board to five, effective immediately.</p>
<p>In a statement, NETCOM said venture investors Lawrence Lepard, 38, general partner of Geocapital Partners and Ofer Nemirovsky, 38, general partner of Hancock Venture Partners Inc.</p>
<p>Both had been original investors in NETCOM, providing venture capital financing prior to the company's December 1994 initial public offering.</p>
